Subject: make_vms.com: on VAX, silence two harmless compiler warnings

zutil.h looks for a 64-bit type by comparing ULONG_MAX and friends with
0xffffffffffffffff. DEC C for VAX cannot represent the constant, warns
(%CC-W-BADHEXCONST) and evaluates the test as false, which is correct
there: VAX has no 64-bit integers.

The VAX C RTL has no vsnprintf(), so gzwrite.c builds gzprintf() as a
stub that returns Z_STREAM_ERROR (rather than the unsafe vsprintf()), and
says so with #warning, which DEC C does not know (%CC-W-BADDIRECTIVE).

MMS stops on either warning status, so disable these two messages on VAX
only. On VAX, gzprintf() therefore always fails; everything else works.
--- a/make_vms.com	2026-11-08 23:09:35.853434022 +0000
+++ b/make_vms.com	2026-11-08 23:09:35.901135966 +0000
@@ -115,6 +115,11 @@
 $       ccopt = ccopt + "/name=as_is/opt=(inline=speed)"
 $       s_case = true
 $   endif
+$! VAX: zutil.h compares limits with 0xffffffffffffffff to look for a 64-bit
+$! type; DEC C for VAX warns that the constant is too large (BADHEXCONST) and
+$! the test is false, which is right there. gzwrite.c uses #warning, which
+$! DEC C does not know (BADDIRECTIVE). MMS stops on either warning.
+$   if vax then ccopt = ccopt + "/warnings=(disable=(badhexconst,baddirective))"
 $ endif
 $ if its_vaxc .or. its_gnuc
 $ then
